{
  "case_id": "2005-04-712",
  "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2005-04-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2600993683-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is a routine diversity case that went seriously awry in the court of appeals. The original defendants in -- named in the complaint, Petitioners State of Wisconsin Investment Board, which I'll refer to as SWIB, and Lincoln Property Company, are completely proper and diverse parties."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Frederick",
      "case_id": "2005-04-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2600993683-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Fourth Circuit's holdings are fundamentally flawed, in two respects."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2600993683-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I thought (b) simply enacted a special necessary condition when you had a local defendant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2600993683-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Frederick, earlier you made the point that Lincoln was a proper \"real party in interest.\" I take it that's not critical to your position."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2600993683-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Did the defendant ever take the position in this litigation, in discovery or anywhere along the line, that they sued their own defendant?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2600993683-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, plaintiff certainly wouldn't want to say there's an indispensable party missing, I take it, because then that would put the plaintiff out of court. The plaintiff is arguing that there's another defendant who should be in here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2005-04-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2600993683-0000-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The real party in interest owns land and operates a substantial part of its business in Virginia, thus establishing a very close nexus with the Commonwealth."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2005-04-712",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2600993683-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the Court has no further questions, thank you."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Gregory P. Joseph",
      "case_id": "2005-04-712",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2600993683-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The judgment of the Fourth Circuit should be affirmed for two reasons, one of which responds to a question that the Chief Justice asked, and that is that Lincoln Property Company was not a real party to the controversy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2005-04-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2600993683-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JOSEPH: Your Honor, we do not, in the sense that we accept the Fourth Circuit's determination that the burden of proof to clarify that entity's status, and the germane entity status"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2600993683-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The \"real party to the controversy\" doctrine is not a new doctrine to this Court. It goes back to at least 1809, Brown against Strode."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2005-04-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2600993683-0002-0005",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Paragraph 22 of their complaint says, and I'll quote, \"All the defendants, acting through Lincoln and/or their obligations as owners of the property through the lease and acting by and through their agents, were responsible for one or more acts of common law and/or statutory negligent conduct with respect to Roche's apartment, including, but not limited to,\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe260099368349792676cfc5a7c6dc23b0ee0ed1cc746c323e5781e7e5033dba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2600993683-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Frederick.\nThe case is submitted.\n[Whereupon, at 11:57 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.]"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
